1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,860
I kick a pebble and it
flies off into the clouds.

3
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:29,360
I was jogging past Kashiwa's gym class,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed,
saying I'm still just as full of energy.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
it's only serious, solid determination.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
One nightmare, the unchanging streetscape,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler, more kind.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,900
the ponzu gives it to us, doesn't it.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Yakitori gushing out,

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,620
is it even worth looking at?

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:04,060
from the waterworks,
the great power lines and the sunset fall.

15
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,060
Tomorrow too,
it'll end with dropping it, won't it.

16
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,740
Published a magazine,
and again they say it's happiness.

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool who only
realized after I lost it.

18
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:27,220
Cycle Big Operation.

19
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,280
Operation Bicycle

20
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,840
What a huge number of bicycles.

21
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:48,080
Are we taking all of them, Kankichi?

22
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,120
Well, if we leave them,
they'll just get in the way of pedestrians.

23
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,560
We'll keep them at the
bicycle impound for a while.

24
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:57,700
If nobody comes to claim them,
they get disposed of.

25
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,060
Are there really bikes
nobody comes to claim?

26
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:05,840
Across the country, about two million
abandoned bicycles are removed every year.

27
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,140
Only about half of their
owners come to pick them up,

28
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:12,260
so about a million get disposed of.

29
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:13,700
That many?

30
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,340
What a waste.

31
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,920
Hey, wait up!

32
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:18,920
What is it?

33
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,600
Could Lemon be wanting
a bicycle or something?

34
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:27,240
She wanted to watch the abandoned
bicycle removal work today, too,

35
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,960
and she even tagged along on purpose.

36
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,640
Now that you mention it, lately she's been

37
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,860
Looks like you've developed
an interest in bicycles.

38
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,840
No doubt about it.

39
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,580
Lemon, you want a bicycle?

40
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:48,780
W-what are you talking about?
Bicycles are expensive!

41
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,860
Hey, to think you'd actually want one...

42
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,980
So you do want one after all.

43
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:53,460
Ugh.

44
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,740
I'll build one for you.

45
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,660
Really, Kankichi?

46
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,140
Yeah, leave it to me.

47
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,680
Hey, are you sure you
can promise that so easily?

48
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:03,805
No need to worry.

49
00:03:03,855 --> 00:03:08,260
After all, a million abandoned
bicycles get scrapped every year.

50
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:13,880
With parts from bikes past their storage period,
I can build as many as I want.

51
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,200
It's done, Lemon!

52
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,140
Well, it's Godzilla again.

53
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,420
There's a name written on it.

54
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:27,440
It has disc brakes on both the front
and back so it can stop right away.

55
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,540
The gears shift automatically.

56
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:32,580
When you pick up speed,
a weight moves and changes the gear.

57
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,920
The frame is carbon and aluminum,
so it's light and doesn't rust.

58
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,560
The wheels are 14-inch magnesium.

59
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:42,560
The training wheels are
2.5-inch German Netzler ones.

60
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,200
Wow.

61
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,360
That sounds pretty amazing.

62
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,900
It really is amazing, this one especially.

63
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,960
And there's a wallet attached
to the back of the saddle!

64
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:55,020
My bicycle always has 30,000 yen in it too.

65
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,200
What's it for?

66
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:00,580
Sometimes you suddenly need
money while you're out, right?

67
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:02,060
Like buying horse betting tickets.

68
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,920
Only you would do that.

69
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,200
Yeah.

70
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:11,680
Alright, that's good.

71
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:23,060
No need. Thanks, Kanchi.

72
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:24,820
Don't mention it.

73
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:35,740
Hey, is Lemon really riding that bike to kindergarten?
At first he just went out to play from Ochanomizu to around Surugadai.

74
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,920
I thought it was odd that he's been
leaving the house so early lately.

75
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,280
So he's been going all the way
to the kindergarten in Ichibanchō?

76
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,820
He actually managed to climb Kudan-zaka?

77
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:50,640
It's a system where the gear ratio
changes when the incline gets steep.

78
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:52,820
Kanda has a lot of slopes, after all.

79
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:55,880
I set it up so even Lemon's
stamina can handle the climb.

80
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:58,260
For a kid's bike, that's pretty high-tech.

81
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:01,240
Thanks to it, Lemon,
who used to love staying indoors,

82
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,360
has become a total outdoorsy type.

83
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:07,160
One of these days, he'll probably ride
his bike all the way to this police box.

84
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,620
No way, he's not like Ryo-chan.

85
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:13,940
Going from Kanda to Kameari
would take hours on a kid's legs.

86
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,780
Yeah, you've got a point.

87
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,020
We came to hang out, Catch!

88
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:24,500
Did you ride a bicycle
all the way from Kanda?

89
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,400
As if I would.

90
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,580
Gepard

91
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:30,600
From there, of course.

92
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,240
You brought the bicycle over in a car?

93
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,660
I'll go for a ride around here.

94
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,260
Don't go too far.

95
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,920
Then I'll come along too.

96
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,800
Ow

97
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,560
I have business with you.

98
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,740
What is it?

99
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,520
I was hoping you'd build me a bicycle.

100
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,520
A bicycle?

101
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,840
You're not planning to ride it yourself,
are you?

102
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,260
Back when I was a schoolgirl,

103
00:05:57,260 --> 00:06:00,080
I used to ride along the
Sumida River all the time.

104
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:16,440
I can't imagine that.

105
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:18,100
Anyway,

106
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:21,540
what I need made is a
delivery bicycle for the shop.

107
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,160
For Kanda Sushi?

108
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:26,480
One of the young guys went out on a delivery the other day,
and it got stolen.

109
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,240
We need a replacement.

110
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,100
Come on, make it right away.

111
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,600
Why do I have to be the one to build it?

112
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,960
Just buy one.

113
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:36,280
I don't want to waste money.

114
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,140
No way, I'm busy here.

115
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,240
You're refusing?

116
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:46,700
How many days is it until
the next payday, again?

117
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:52,520
Lately,
whenever you run out of money before payday,

118
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,980
you come over to our place to eat.

119
00:06:54,980 --> 00:07:00,580
One word from me and I can
ban you from coming here!

120
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:05,420
Damn it, she's hitting me where it hurts.

121
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:07,560
You'll make it, won't you?

122
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:12,760
Fine, fine, I'll make it, okay?

123
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,600
Just make one that can never be stolen.

124
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,040
It's done!

125
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,960
Which one?

126
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,540
Ta-da!

127
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,260
The bicycle that can never be stolen!

128
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:27,920
Isn't it? But this saddle here -

129
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:36,160
it's a jug-stand type. If you carry the saddle around, no one can ride off with it.
And the handlebars, pedals, and tires too,

130
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:42,540
if you carry them all like this, no one will ever bother with them.
Hey, it's all falling apart!

131
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:53,640
A bicycle that can never be stolen! Plus, you can fit a battery to the bike.
If someone accidentally tries to take it, they'll get an electric shock.

132
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:55,420
You love it, don't you?

133
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,500
The only flaw is that when it rains,

134
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:59,080
Whoa!

135
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,060
Oh no...

136
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,380
Forgive me!

137
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,700
That's dangerous!

138
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:05,420
There's more, I tell you!

139
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:07,780
Number three.

140
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,480
This is a simple, easy anti-theft method.

141
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:17,960
You just tape thumbtacks painted black
with a marker to the saddle like this.

142
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:20,420
It's a cheap, easy guerrilla tactic.

143
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,360
Sure, it's easy, I'll give you that.

144
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:26,040
Listen, don't forget they're
there if you're spacing out.

145
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,820
Lemon's late

146
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,380
What, he still hasn't come back?

147
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,160
I'm a little worried, you know.

148
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,340
Alright, I'll go run and look for him.

149
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:37,040
Up we go.

150
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,100
What a silly boy.

151
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:43,580
Lemon!

152
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,740
Thank goodness, you're safe!

153
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,880
Your bicycle...

154
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,280
I see.

155
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:58,100
So it was stolen while
you were in the toilet?

156
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,000
Damn it!

157
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:03,360
I should've taken better
anti-theft measures on Lemon's bike.

158
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,880
I'm sorry, Kankichi.

159
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,200
Lemon, you have nothing to apologize for.

160
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,200
The one to blame is the thief.

161
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,340
That's right.

162
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:13,540
We'll get it back, no matter what.

163
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,680
Kankichi.

164
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:15,720
Matoi.

165
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:22,380
It's a conspicuous bike,
so someone may have seen it.

166
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,220
Let's go ask around a bit.

167
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:39,100
No clues here either.

168
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:41,280
What do we do, Kankichi?

169
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,840
My bicycle's gone!

170
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,020
It was locked up, you know!

171
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,637
Damn it! Not only Lemon's bike,

172
00:09:50,687 --> 00:09:53,020
but mine has been stolen too!

173
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:57,840
It looks like the other bikes are gone too.

174
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,840
Come to think of it.

175
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:03,200
Kankichi! Look!

176
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,240
Whoa!

177
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:08,920
They mistook it for an abandoned
bicycle and hauled it away.

178
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,080
Hey, wait! My bicycle!

179
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,520
Damn it!

180
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,900
Hey! What's going on here?!

181
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,540
What is it, caveman?

182
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:25,300
It's not a joke! I used that for work. Give
it back right now! There was 30,000 yen in it!

183
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:37,340
Wait, what are you talking about? My bike was removed along with other bicycles.
When did this happen? Just now, on the shopping street!

184
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,700
That's strange.

185
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,160
What's strange about it?

186
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,640
The removed bicycles are being carried away.

187
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,220
I saw it with my own eyes too,

188
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:48,000
but today,

189
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,320
we aren't scheduled to
remove any abandoned bicycles.

190
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,020
What?

191
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,020
Senpai

192
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,040
Honda

193
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,580
Snap out of it, Honda!

194
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:06,120
What happened?

195
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:07,680
The Shiraume!

196
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,080
The Shiraume!

197
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,500
But while I was taking a
little break in Kanamachi,

198
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:18,400
they hauled the Shiraume away,
so I had to walk back.

199
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,320
They actually removed the Shiraume?

200
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,520
That's ridiculous!

201
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,460
Could this be...

202
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,080
Ryo-sama?

203
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:28,900
Disguised as the removal
of abandoned bicycles,

204
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:32,820
there must be someone stealing
bicycles and motorcycles!

205
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:39,440
My bicycle, Honda's motorcycle,
and Lemon's bicycle were all stolen by them!

206
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,180
I won't forgive this.

207
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:44,300
I'll catch them, no matter what!

208
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:01,560
The places with lots of abandoned
bicycles are marked in red.

209
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:05,660
I contacted our colleagues on
patrol and gathered information.

210
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:09,260
And this is where the bicycles
disappeared in bulk today.

211
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,400
Here.

212
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,160
Here.

213
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,400
This is where mine was taken.

214
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,940
Mine was taken here.

215
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:17,660
Yeah.

216
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:21,780
If that's the case,
the next place they'll target is likely

217
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,920
here, then.

218
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:25,640
Exactly, Lemon.

219
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:28,300
Should we lie in wait
and catch the culprits?

220
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,591
No, these guys pull off
something this large-scale.

221
00:12:31,641 --> 00:12:35,460
They must have a hideout somewhere.
We'll track it down.

222
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:37,720
Ohh.

223
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,200
A caveman is saying something sensible.

224
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,280
He sounds just like a police officer.

225
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,280
Kankichi is a bona fide police officer,
you know.

226
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:50,153
Ahaha. Y-yes, that's right, isn't it.

227
00:12:50,203 --> 00:12:52,500
Do you have some good plan?

228
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:55,440
Hey, leave it to me.

229
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,420
Senpai, can you hear me?

230
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:16,400
Reception is good.

231
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:20,820
You'd better be properly monitoring
our position on your end, too.

232
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:25,200
You're showing up clearly.

233
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,660
Don't lose sight of us.

234
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,180
Yes.

235
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,280
Here it comes.

236
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:50,660
You, hurry up.

237
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:15,080
Damn it, handle it more carefully!

238
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,080
Tch!

239
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:25,620
Hey!

240
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,160
Police! Let's do this.

241
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,740
W-what is it?

242
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:36,160
The truck's getting away!

243
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:38,020
What?

244
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:39,060
Hmph.

245
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,640
Reiko-san, are you all right?

246
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:56,360
Even so, pursuing them is impossible now.

247
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,840
I'm leaving the rest to you.

248
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,200
Understood, leave it to me.

249
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,260
The culprits went that way!

250
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:06,480
Looks like they're
heading for the expressway.

251
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:09,900
Hey, we'll catch up to them
at the expressway entrance!

252
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,260
Ouch!

253
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:23,280
Here they come again!

254
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,520
Do you think I'll fall
for the same trick again?

255
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,440
Damn it!

256
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,240
Damn it.

257
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:46,240
They're really going a long way.

258
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:55,540
Damn, they shook us off!

259
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,660
Hey, wait! I'm falling behind!

260
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:03,540
Damn, don't they notice?

261
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,060
At this rate, we'll lose them!

262
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:13,560
There!

263
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:19,180
Damn! We're out of gas!

264
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:25,640
Fill it up with regular.

265
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,480
It talked!

266
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,460
Hurry up.

267
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:29,320
Yes.

268
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:35,420
Send the bill to Katsushika Station.

269
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:41,360
Damn, we have to catch up fast!

270
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:42,880
There it is!

271
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,780
What's wrong, old man?

272
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:56,180
I asked what's wrong, hurry up!

273
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,720
I twisted my ankle, so...

274
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,140
Geez, where's your home?

275
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,180
It's just right over there.

276
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:08,960
That close

277
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,460
Got it.

278
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,340
Hop on! I'll take you there!

279
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:18,260
Hold on tight!

280
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:22,080
Grandpa!

281
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:25,694
Grandpa,

282
00:17:25,744 --> 00:17:27,840
What was that?

283
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:30,542
He just took me home.

284
00:17:30,592 --> 00:17:32,420
Thank you, thank you.

285
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,240
Move! Move! Move! Move! Move!

286
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,600
Damn, on a night road like this!

287
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:39,720
Get out of the way! Move!

288
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,540
I'm the number one on this pass.

289
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,140
No, I'm the number one!

290
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:52,500
What?

291
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,180
A monkey just passed me.

292
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,580
It's a nightmare.

293
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,520
We finally caught up.

294
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,860
Looks like this is their hideout.

295
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,020
Honda, can you hear me?

296
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,660
Honda, Honda!

297
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:25,880
What's going on?

298
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:31,660
Senpai, please answer me, senpai.

299
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:33,580
Did something happen to Lemon?

300
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:37,200
It's fine, I'm sure the radio just broke.

301
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,520
That guy won't go down that easily.

302
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:42,320
Yeah.

303
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,340
We know where they are.

304
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:45,620
We'll be there right away.

305
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:53,020
W-what is this?

306
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,980
So they've stolen this many?

307
00:18:57,580 --> 00:19:00,380
Are these the ones who stole
the commissioners' bicycles too?

308
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:05,240
Come to think of it,
there should've been a big motorcycle here.

309
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:06,860
What?

310
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,940
Lemon's bicycle is -

311
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:13,060
Here it is!

312
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,920
And my bicycle?

313
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,080
Boss.

314
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:20,160
So that guy's the boss?

315
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,940
Hmph, they've gathered quite a lot.

316
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:25,400
Japanese people are strange, you know.

317
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:27,420
When a bicycle gets hauled away,

318
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:29,200
they just assume it's their own fault

319
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,540
and don't even bother filing a report.

320
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,640
That leaves them free to
sell them off without a worry.

321
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:37,960
Damn, what a bastard.

322
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:45,320
The ones that won't sell, melt them down in the back furnace.
Don't leave any evidence, got it, boss.

323
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:49,740
Stuff like this won't sell, right?
My bicycle.

324
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:54,360
A police bicycle. This is rare.

325
00:19:55,180 --> 00:20:04,160
It won't sell, but let's add it to my collection with that motorcycle cop bike from earlier.
No way! My 30,000 yen is in there!

326
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:06,660
Boss, how about this one?

327
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,400
Burger.

328
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:11,640
That kind of thing won't sell.

329
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:13,860
But it looks pretty expensive, though.

330
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:15,840
It's custom-made to size.

331
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:18,820
There's only one,
so it'll be traced right away.

332
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:19,840
I see.

333
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:21,760
Melt it down later.

334
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:22,900
First, food.

335
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:27,100
We'll do it tonight,
my bicycle and Lemon's...

336
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:31,400
Honda

337
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,220
Honda

338
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:34,880
It's no use after all!

339
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,960
We have to call for backup somehow,
and fast!

340
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,200
Hey, didn't I just hear a
voice from inside the warehouse?

341
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:45,140
You imagined it, right? You're just tired.

342
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:47,600
Yeah, maybe I did imagine it.

343
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:51,900
But I'll check just in case.

344
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:57,540
Aaaaaaah!

345
00:21:02,740 --> 00:21:03,580
Which one?

346
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:05,800
No, no.

347
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:08,820
It's Doamasu.

348
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:10,540
Doamasu has appeared!

349
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,320
Uh-oh.

350
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,920
Where are my and Lemon's bicycles?

351
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,240
Which one?

352
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:26,180
What?

353
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,860
What, the bike has a face?

354
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,820
I'm placing you under arrest!

355
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,380
The bike talked!

356
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:37,640
Like hell I'll let him get away!

357
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,960
My bicycle!

358
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:43,220
Won't let him...

359
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:50,680
Damn it, my 30,000 yen...

360
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:56,220
That's Lemon's bicycle.

361
00:21:56,220 --> 00:21:58,400
At this rate, we're done for.

362
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:03,360
Aaaaaah!

363
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:33,320
Go for it!

364
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:43,740
Wait!

365
00:22:58,220 --> 00:23:00,160
Somehow, I'm safe,

366
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:00,760
Senpai

367
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:01,360
Yes!

368
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:03,140
Kankichi!

369
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:05,660
Lemon! Matoi! Honda!

370
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:08,580
Senpai, are you all right?

371
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:10,500
So you're safe!

372
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:11,740
Here you go.

373
00:23:11,740 --> 00:23:12,480
Whoa!

374
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:19,160
Thank you, Kankichi!
I won't lose it ever again!

375
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:20,920
Huh?

376
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:26,320
It feels like I'm forgetting
something important...

377
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:29,900
Kankichi? Could that be yours...

378
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:37,340
My bicycle, the 30,000 yen one...

379
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:41,580
Don't stop me!

380
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,860
Let me pull back!

381
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:46,280
30,000 yen!

382
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:04,480
Walking along,
led by the hand of the gacha machine,

383
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:11,660
the strange feeling I had back then

384
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:16,900
so I walked along the arcade's guide tiles,

385
00:24:17,580 --> 00:24:22,660
stepping only on the black parts.

386
00:24:25,540 --> 00:24:28,860
Everyone was a child once,

387
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,980
but the politicians with their smug faces,

388
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,260
and the aunties who
are a thorn in your side,

389
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:41,280
why not take a turn?

390
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:43,860
Around that corner,

391
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:49,040
you'll meet everyone, everyone.

392
00:24:51,020 --> 00:24:53,640
Over there is Kameari,

393
00:24:54,740 --> 00:24:57,000
surely Kameari,

394
00:24:58,280 --> 00:25:02,200
everyone, come to our town!

395
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:06,900
Over there is Kameari,

396
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:10,180
surely Kameari,

397
00:25:11,060 --> 00:25:15,440
everyone, come to our town!

398
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:17,020
Thank you.

399
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,640
Yay! The annoying Chief isn't here today!

400
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:27,300
That means I'm the most important
person at the station, right?

401
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:30,120
Alright, I'll take command, then.

402
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:33,160
Why are Matei, Komachi, and Naoko here?

403
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:37,020
Next time: Women-Only Police Box.
See you then!

404
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:39,520
Thank you.

405
00:25:53,640 --> 00:25:53,940
Thanks for watching.

